// Story settings: genre, tone, stakes, era, authors and writing style. These belong to the whole chat.
// Each option is one line of fields:
//   id      never change it: saved chats store values under it
//   label   the name in the panel
//   cue     the plain description Claude reads
//   note    (optional) longer text shown in the panel only
//   prompt  (optional) the wording sent: true means "label: cue" (label in lower case), or the exact text
//   onPage  (optional) how the feeling shows in voice, body and choices; sent with the feeling
// Authors also have:
//   books   one or two of their best-known books, shown in the panel only (never sent)
//   style   how they write, as "Narration: \u2026 Dialogue: \u2026"; sent as is, and shown in the panel
// An author's cue is technique only (sentence shape, point of view, rhythm, what gets dwelt on), never their
// plots or characters, so the voice carries into any story.
// Each group's order number sets where it sits in the panel (authors come right after the writing groups).

